          %h2#section_Idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em walking equivalence
            (as in “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+structure"}> walking structure
            ”) or
            %em free-standing equivalence
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            (in fact a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalences
            in a 2-category. It is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free-standing+isomorphism"} free-standing isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+adjoint+equivalence"} walking adjoint equivalence
            is another.
          %p
            Roughly speaking, it is the minimal 2-category which contains a 1-arrow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            with an inverse-up-to-isomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-isomorphism"} 2-isomorphism
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g f
            and the identity, and a 2-isomorphism between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f g
            and the identity.
          %p
            The
            %em walking semi-strict equivalence
            is the same except that either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f g
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g f
            is required to be equal on the nose to the identity.
          %p
          %h2#section_Definitions Definitions
          %p
          #DefinitionFreeStandingEquivalence.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{\leq 1}
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
              with exactly two objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: 0 \rightarrow 1
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^{-1}: 1 \rightarrow 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              be the free strict 2-category on the 2-truncated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+globular+set"} reflexive globular set
              whose 1-truncation is the underlying reflexive directed graph of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≤
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{\leq 1}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_{0}: i^{-1} \circ i \rightarrow id(0)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ι
                        %mn 0
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_{0}^{-1}: id(0) \rightarrow i^{-1} \circ i
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∘
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_{1}: i \circ i^{-1} \rightarrow id(1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ι
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∘
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_{1}^{-1}: i \circ i^{-1} \rightarrow id(1)
            %p
              The
              %em free-standing equivalence
              is the quotient
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              by the relation on 2-arrows generated by forcing the equations
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi ι
                        %mn 0
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_{0}^{-1} \circ \iota_{0} = id
              = succeed "," do
